From a6cc3dd9901cdfeb18dd8a6fb228a063e450b9a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:15:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] downloads: fall back to copy+delete when SAF
 renameDocument is unsupported

ZhuoyiTong (HarmonyOS Android compatibility container) exposes a
DocumentsProvider that does not implement renameDocument(). Mihon finalises
every downloaded page and chapter directory with UniFile.renameTo(), so on
those devices images stay as *.tmp and the chapter download fails.

Add UniFile.renameToOrCopy(): try renameTo() first and, when it fails, copy
the file or directory tree to the destination and delete the source.
Downloader uses it for page files, the chapter directory and the CBZ
archive. Devices whose provider supports rename keep the original path.

Based on zsyou/mihon-harmony (.github/patches/harmony.patch plus the
Downloader.kt edits in its release workflow); upstream PR
https://github.com/mihonapp/mihon/pull/3446.
